---
title: "Access setup order: GitHub OAuth App, then IdP, then policy, then Access apps"
---
flowchart LR
  github["1. GitHub UI<br/>Register OAuth App<br/>no REST create"]
  idp["2. Zero Trust IdP<br/>paste Client ID + secret<br/>authorize orgs + email"]
  policy["3. Allow policy<br/>GitHub org = your-org<br/>reuse on both hosts"]
  apps["4. Access apps<br/>custom domain<br/>and pages.dev"]
  warning["Do not start at step 4<br/>Access applications deny by default<br/>without an IdP and Allow policy"]
  github --> idp --> policy --> apps
  warning -.-> apps
  class github success
  class idp,policy primary
  class apps secondary
  class warning danger
  accTitle: Access setup order: GitHub OAuth App, then IdP, then policy, then Access apps
  accDescr: Do not create Access applications first. They deny by default. Register the GitHub OAuth App in GitHub's UI (no API), add it as a Zero Trust identity provider, write the Allow policy, then attach Access apps to both hostnames.

  classDef primary fill:#ffffff,stroke:#2c2c2c,color:#1a1a1a,stroke-width:2px
